WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.680 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  Sunday afternoon in the city of Chetumal  in southeastern Mexico a chance to spend  time with the family and let someone  else do the cooking on weekends there  are lots of tasty treats on offer here  are all in one take home runs a popular  stand his speciality tacos el Pasto  Shepherd style before it lands on the  grill the pork is marinated in pineapple  dried chilies and spices  it's served on tortillas or with bread  a generous squeeze of lime juice and  they're ready to go  some like a sprinkle of onions and  coriander too so delicious why flavor is  sensational the pineapple the lime it's  something special there's an array of  extra sauces and toppings and Raul has  other meats we serve paprika sausage  marinated pork and cutlets and for the  discerning palate bachata fine skirt  steak customers often order as many as  seven different kinds of tacos each one  costs 60 Euro cents the meat is really  good the sauce is a special blend of  spices not too hot the pork is nicely  browned hardly any other stand has such  a variety of sauces and veggie toppings  on offer it's so good even after  nightfall the customers keep coming top  seller is pork tacos al pastor it's  something you'll find everywhere you  find it all over Mexico everybody likes  it visitors tourists everyone and Raul  will serve many more before the day is  done

